Ticket **#4471** holds 412 unique reports about dates landing on the wrong day. The desk
merged them as one known issue and queued one fix. The export’s own cause logic shows that is
wrong: the reports are two different bugs that share a subject line.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one problem. Subject-line dedupe put two causes in one ticket.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Problems to file

1. **parser** — the shared parser reads every date month-first. Day-first tenants (app, email,
   and booking-v2 forms) get month and day flipped. This is the majority of #4471.
2. **hint** — booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, so people type month-first,
   while the form still reads the tenant’s day-first locale. That is a different bug. It has no
   ticket of its own.

Each cause needs its own ticket, with the report count the table computes above. Do not treat
the one-day-move footnotes as a third cause: those five reports are still `parser` by tenant.

## Why the merge happened

Triage matches on subject alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). Same
wording, different cause — still merged. Intake tags also disagree with the real cause often
enough that a tag is not enough to split on.

